+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Asks for the conversations the connection's own user holds. The frame carries paging and nothing else: there is no user id field, because the list is never anyone else's. The server reads the user from the authenticated connection and never from the frame, so a `userId` a client puts on it is dropped by the validator and `listFor` is called with the socket's own user ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": { "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:05:00.000Z", "sessionId": "s3" }
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                                          |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_sessions"`                                                     |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | Non-negative integer; how many summaries to answer                    |
+| `before` | object | No       | Cursor of the last row seen: `{ updatedAt, sessionId }`, both halved  |
+
+Constraints:
+
+- `limit`, when present, MUST be a non-negative integer; `before`, when present, MUST be an object whose `sessionId` is a string of 1 to 128 characters and whose `updatedAt` is a string or number that parses as a moment. Any other `list_sessions` payload is refused with `INVALID_MESSAGE` naming the field, and the session store is not asked ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L135)).
+- The validator answers a valid frame with the `limit` and `before` the frame names and nothing else it carries ([validated by: answers a valid frame with the limit and cursor it names and nothing else it carries](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L31)).
+- A `limit` that is not a non-negative integer — a string, a fraction, a negative one, not a number at all — is refused with an error naming `limit` ([validated by: rejects a limit that is not a non-negative integer, naming the field](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L43)).
+- A `before` the validator cannot read is refused with an error naming the half that failed ([validated by: rejects a cursor it cannot page by, naming the field it fails on](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L51)).
+
+The frame is validated whether or not the session store implements `listFor`; validation is static and reads no configuration. The answer is carried by `session_list` (Section 5.9). A `list_sessions` is not a turn: it is answered off the per-session lock that serialises `user_message` frames, and no `stream_end` follows it. Off that lock a socket's frames are still answered in the order they arrived, so a `ping` sent after a `list_sessions` is answered after the list's answer and a client can drain on its own heartbeat ([validated by: answers a ping sent after a list_sessions after the list answer, while both still bypass the turn lock](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L873)).
