+### 5.9 session_list
+
+The answer to a `list_sessions` frame (Section 4.3): one row per conversation the connection's user holds. It is not part of any stream — no `entry_commit` precedes it and no `stream_end` follows it; the frame exchange is exactly the request and this reply ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "session_list",
+  "sessions": [
+    {
+      "sessionId": "s1",
+      "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:01:00.000Z",
+      "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:05:00.000Z",
+      "entryCount": 6
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+| Field                   | Type    | Description                                            |
+| ----------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `type`                  | string  | `"session_list"`                                       |
+| `sessions`              | array   | One row per conversation, newest first                 |
+| `sessions[].sessionId`  | string  | Conversation identifier, usable on `?sessionId=` reconnect |
+| `sessions[].createdAt`  | string  | ISO 8601 timestamp                                     |
+| `sessions[].updatedAt`  | string  | ISO 8601 timestamp; doubles as the paging key          |
+| `sessions[].entryCount` | number  | How many entries the conversation holds                |
